    "faq": {
      "type":"suntneew-pdp-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"How much energy does the 314Ah battery store?","answer":"<p>The rated energy is 4,019.2Wh from the documented 12.8V and 314Ah ratings. Actual usable energy depends on operating limits, load and system settings.</p>"}},
        "q2":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What is the difference between 157A and 200A?","answer":"<p>157A is the maximum continuous charge/discharge value used for normal system sizing. 200A is the BMS protection threshold, not a continuous operating rating. Use 63A as the recommended charge-current reference and size every system component to its lowest limit.</p>"}},
        "q3":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Can the 314Ah battery use the same compartment as the 230Ah model?","answer":"<p>The stated 522 × 268 × 220 mm enclosure dimensions are the same, but the 314Ah battery weighs 26kg. Recheck structure, restraint, access and the complete electrical design for the exact model.</p>"}},
        "q4":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What does IP65 mean for this battery?","answer":"<p>IP65 indicates a dust-tight enclosure with protection against water jets. It is not an immersion rating; keep the battery location, terminals and cable routing protected and follow the installation manual.</p>"}},
        "q5":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Should I choose the 314Ah or 230Ah battery?","answer":"<p>Choose 314Ah when 2,010W covers your simultaneous load and you want 1,075.2Wh / 36.5% more reserve in the same 522 × 268 × 220mm enclosure. Choose 230Ah when 2,944Wh covers your time between charges and you want 2,560W continuous output, 5.4kg less weight and the lower current single-unit price. Test your devices in the <a href=\"/pages/power-calculator?scenario=rv\">Power Planner</a>.</p>"}},
        "q6":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Where can I review the complete operating limits?","answer":"<p>The current English product manual is available in Documents on this page. Review it together with the charger, inverter and RV manufacturer instructions before installation.</p>"}}
      },
